<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Parliamentary Voting Record — Fiji Political Review</title>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Libre+Baskerville:ital,wght@0,400;0,700;1,400&family=Source+Sans+3:wght@300;400;500;600&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<style>
*, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
:root {
  --teal: #1D6A72; --teal-dark: #155860; --teal-light: #E0F2F3;
  --gold: #C8982A; --gold-light: #FDF5E4;
  --navy: #1B2A4A;
  --red: #A32D2D; --red-light: #FCEBEB;
  --green: #3B6D11; --green-light: #EAF3DE;
  --amber: #854F0B; --amber-light: #FAEEDA;
  --blue: #185FA5; --blue-light: #E6F1FB;
  --grey: #F5F5F3; --border: #E2E2DE;
  --text: #1A1A1A; --text-mid: #555550; --text-muted: #888882;
  --white: #FFFFFF;
}
body { font-family: 'Source Sans 3', sans-serif; font-size: 15px; color: var(--text); background: var(--white); line-height: 1.6; -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased; }

/* Header */
.site-header { background: var(--teal); padding: 0 24px; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--gold); }
.header-inner { max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; height: 52px; }
.site-name { font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif; font-size: 16px; color: white; text-decoration: none; }
.header-label { font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.55); }

/* Hero */
.hero { background: var(--navy); padding: 40px 24px 36px; border-bottom: 3px solid var(--gold); }
.hero-inner { max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; }
.hero-eyebrow { font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--gold); font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 10px; }
.hero-title { font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif; font-size: clamp(20px, 3vw, 28px); color: white; line-height: 1.3; margin-bottom: 10px; font-weight: 700; }
.hero-desc { font-size: 14px; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.6); max-width: 700px; line-height: 1.65; margin-bottom: 24px; }
.hero-stats { display: flex; gap: 32px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
.hero-stat { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2px; }
.hero-stat-num { font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif; font-size: 24px; font-weight: 700; color: white; }
.hero-stat-label { font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.06em; text-transform: uppercase; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.4); }

/* Tabs */
.tabs { background: var(--grey); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 0 24px; position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 90; }
.tabs-inner { max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; display: flex; gap: 0; }
.tab { padding: 14px 20px; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 500; color: var(--text-mid); cursor: pointer; border-bottom: 2px solid transparent; border: none; background: none; font-family: 'Source Sans 3', sans-serif; transition: all 0.15s; white-space: nowrap; }
.tab:hover { color: var(--teal); }
.tab.active { color: var(--teal); border-bottom: 2px solid var(--teal); }

/* Main */
.main { max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 28px 24px 80px; }

/* Controls */
.controls { display: flex; gap: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 20px; align-items: center; }
.search-input { flex: 1; min-width: 200px; max-width: 320px; padding: 8px 12px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 6px; font-size: 13px; font-family: 'Source Sans 3', sans-serif; background: white; color: var(--text); outline: none; }
.search-input:focus { border-color: var(--teal); }
.select-filter { padding: 7px 12px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 6px; font-size: 13px; font-family: 'Source Sans 3', sans-serif; background: white; color: var(--text); outline: none; cursor: pointer; }
.select-filter:focus { border-color: var(--teal); }
.results-info { font-size: 12px; color: var(--text-muted); margin-left: auto; }

/* Votes Table View */
.view { display: none; }
.view.active { display: block; }

/* Vote cards */
.vote-card { border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; margin-bottom: 10px; }
.vote-card.hidden { display: none; }
.vote-header { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 14px; padding: 14px 16px; cursor: pointer; background: white; transition: background 0.1s; }
.vote-header:hover { background: #FAFAF8; }
.vote-header.open { background: #FAFAF8; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
.vote-date { font-size: 11px; color: var(--text-muted); white-space: nowrap; min-width: 80px; padding-top: 3px; }
.vote-info { flex: 1; }
.vote-title { font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text); margin-bottom: 4px; line-height: 1.4; }
.vote-meta { font-size: 12px; color: var(--text-muted); }
.vote-result { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-end; gap: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; }
.result-badge { font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; padding: 3px 10px; border-radius: 4px; white-space: nowrap; }
.result-passed { background: var(--green-light); color: var(--green); }
.result-failed { background: var(--red-light); color: var(--red); }
.result-withdrawn { background: var(--amber-light); color: var(--amber); }
.vote-tally { font-size: 12px; color: var(--text-muted); }
.chevron { font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-muted); transition: transform 0.2s; flex-shrink: 0; padding-top: 2px; }
.chevron.open { transform: rotate(90deg); }

/* Vote body */
.vote-body { display: none; background: white; }
.vote-body.open { display: block; }
.vote-summary { padding: 14px 16px 14px 110px; background: #F9F9F7; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); font-size: 13px; color: var(--text-mid); line-height: 1.65; font-style: italic; font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif; }
.vote-detail { padding: 14px 16px 14px 110px; }
.detail-label { font-size: 10px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--teal); margin-bottom: 8px; }
.mp-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(180px, 1fr)); gap: 6px; margin-bottom: 14px; }
.mp-vote { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; padding: 6px 10px; border-radius: 5px; font-size: 12px; }
.mp-vote.aye { background: var(--green-light); }
.mp-vote.no { background: var(--red-light); }
.mp-vote.abstain { background: var(--amber-light); }
.mp-vote.absent { background: var(--grey); }
.mp-dot { width: 8px; height: 8px; border-radius: 50%; flex-shrink: 0; }
.mp-dot.aye { background: var(--green); }
.mp-dot.no { background: var(--red); }
.mp-dot.abstain { background: var(--amber); }
.mp-dot.absent { background: var(--text-muted); }
.mp-name { font-weight: 500; color: var(--text); }
.mp-party { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 11px; }
.vote-analysis { padding: 10px 14px; border-left: 3px solid var(--teal); background: var(--teal-light); border-radius: 0 5px 5px 0; font-size: 13px; color: var(--teal-dark); line-height: 1.6; margin-top: 4px; }
.vote-analysis-label { font-size: 10px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--teal); margin-bottom: 3px; }
.vote-tags { display: flex; gap: 5px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 10px; }
.vtag { font-size: 11px; padding: 2px 7px; border-radius: 3px; background: var(--grey); color: var(--text-mid); border: 1px solid var(--border); }
.data-note { padding: 8px 12px; background: var(--amber-light); border-left: 3px solid var(--gold); border-radius: 0 5px 5px 0; font-size: 12px; color: var(--amber); margin-top: 10px; }

/* MP Tracker View */
.mp-list { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(280px, 1fr)); gap: 12px; }
.mp-card { border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; cursor: pointer; transition: border-color 0.15s; }
.mp-card:hover { border-color: var(--teal); }
.mp-card-header { padding: 14px; background: var(--grey); display: flex; gap: 12px; align-items: center; }
.mp-avatar { width: 36px; height: 36px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--teal); display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 700; color: white; flex-shrink: 0; }
.mp-card-name { font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text); }
.mp-card-role { font-size: 11px; color: var(--text-muted); }
.mp-card-party { display: inline-block; font-size: 10px; font-weight: 600; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 3px; margin-top: 2px; }
.party-PA { background: #DBEAFE; color: #1E40AF; }
.party-NFP { background: #FCE7F3; color: #9D174D; }
.party-SODELPA { background: #D1FAE5; color: #065F46; }
.party-FijiFirst { background: #FEF3C7; color: #92400E; }
.party-IND { background: var(--grey); color: var(--text-muted); }
.mp-card-body { padding: 12px 14px; }
.mp-stat-row { display: flex; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 8px; }
.mp-stat { text-align: center; flex: 1; }
.mp-stat-num { font-size: 18px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text); }
.mp-stat-num.green { color: var(--green); }
.mp-stat-num.red { color: var(--red); }
.mp-stat-num.amber { color: var(--amber); }
.mp-stat-num.grey { color: var(--text-muted); }
.mp-stat-label { font-size: 10px; color: var(--text-muted); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; }
.attend-bar { height: 6px; border-radius: 3px; background: var(--border); overflow: hidden; }
.attend-fill { height: 100%; border-radius: 3px; background: var(--teal); }

/* Legend */
.legend { display: flex; gap: 16px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 16px; }
.legend-item { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; font-size: 12px; color: var(--text-mid); }
.legend-dot { width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 50%; }

/* Party filter pills */
.party-pills { display: flex; gap: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 16px; }
.party-pill { padding: 4px 12px; font-size: 12px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 20px; background: white; color: var(--text-mid); cursor: pointer; font-family: 'Source Sans 3', sans-serif; font-weight: 500; transition: all 0.15s; }
.party-pill:hover { border-color: var(--teal); color: var(--teal); }
.party-pill.active { background: var(--teal); color: white; border-color: var(--teal); }

/* About view */
.about-box { background: var(--grey); border-radius: 8px; padding: 24px; margin-bottom: 20px; }
.about-box h3 { font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif; font-size: 16px; color: var(--navy); margin-bottom: 10px; }
.about-box p { font-size: 13px; color: var(--text-mid); line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 10px; }
.about-box p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
.methodology-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(220px, 1fr)); gap: 12px; margin-top: 16px; }
.method-card { background: white; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 6px; padding: 14px; }
.method-card h4 { font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--navy); margin-bottom: 6px; }
.method-card p { font-size: 12px; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.6; }

/* No results */
.no-results { text-align: center; padding: 40px; color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 14px; display: none; }

/* Footer */
.tool-footer { background: var(--navy); padding: 20px 24px; text-align: center; }
.tool-footer p { font-size: 12px; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.4); max-width: 700px; margin: 0 auto; line-height: 1.7; }
.tool-footer a { color: var(--gold); text-decoration: none; }

@media (max-width: 640px) {
  .hero { padding: 28px 16px; }
  .main { padding: 20px 16px 60px; }
  .vote-summary, .vote-detail { padding-left: 16px; }
  .mp-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
  .hero-stats { gap: 20px; }
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<header class="site-header">
  <div class="header-inner">
    <a href="https://fijipoliticalreview.com" class="site-name">Fiji Political Review</a>
    <span class="header-label">Parliamentary Watch</span>
  </div>
</header>

<div class="hero">
  <div class="hero-inner">
    <div class="hero-eyebrow">Parliamentary Voting Record — 2022–2027 Parliament</div>
    <h1 class="hero-title">How Did Your MP Vote?</h1>
    <p class="hero-desc">Every significant parliamentary division since the December 2022 election — tracked by MP, party and bill. Fiji's parliament does not make this easy to find. The FPR makes it easy.</p>
    <div class="hero-stats">
      <div class="hero-stat"><span class="hero-stat-num" id="stat-votes">12</span><span class="hero-stat-label">Votes tracked</span></div>
      <div class="hero-stat"><span class="hero-stat-num" id="stat-mps">55</span><span class="hero-stat-label">MPs covered</span></div>
      <div class="hero-stat"><span class="hero-stat-num" id="stat-sessions">8</span><span class="hero-stat-label">Parliamentary sessions</span></div>
      <div class="hero-stat"><span class="hero-stat-num" id="stat-updated">May 2026</span><span class="hero-stat-label">Last updated</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="tabs">
  <div class="tabs-inner">
    <button class="tab active" onclick="switchTab('votes', this)">All Votes</button>
    <button class="tab" onclick="switchTab('mps', this)">By MP</button>
    <button class="tab" onclick="switchTab('about', this)">Methodology</button>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="main">

  <!-- ═══ VOTES VIEW ═══ -->
  <div class="view active" id="view-votes">

    <div class="controls">
      <input type="text" class="search-input" id="vote-search" placeholder="Search bills or votes..." oninput="filterVotes()">
      <select class="select-filter" id="vote-category" onchange="filterVotes()">
        <option value="all">All categories</option>
        <option value="budget">Budget and finance</option>
        <option value="constitutional">Constitutional</option>
        <option value="governance">Governance</option>
        <option value="social">Social policy</option>
        <option value="electoral">Electoral</option>
      </select>
      <select class="select-filter" id="vote-result" onchange="filterVotes()">
        <option value="all">All outcomes</option>
        <option value="passed">Passed</option>
        <option value="failed">Failed</option>
      </select>
      <span class="results-info" id="vote-count"></span>
    </div>

    <div class="legend">
      <div class="legend-item"><div class="legend-dot" style="background:var(--green)"></div>Aye</div>
      <div class="legend-item"><div class="legend-dot" style="background:var(--red)"></div>No</div>
      <div class="legend-item"><div class="legend-dot" style="background:var(--amber)"></div>Abstain</div>
      <div class="legend-item"><div class="legend-dot" style="background:var(--text-muted)"></div>Absent</div>
    </div>

    <div id="votes-list">

      <!-- VOTE 1 -->
      <div class="vote-card" data-category="budget" data-result="passed" data-text="2023 budget appropriation bill fiscal year">
        <div class="vote-header" onclick="toggleVote(this)">
          <span class="vote-date">24 Nov 2023</span>
          <div class="vote-info">
            <div class="vote-title">Appropriation (2023-2024) Bill — Second Reading</div>
            <div class="vote-meta">Budget and finance · Session 3, 2023</div>
          </div>
          <div class="vote-result">
            <span class="result-badge result-passed">Passed</span>
            <span class="vote-tally">Ayes 28 · Noes 18 · Absent 9</span>
          </div>
          <span class="chevron">›</span>
        </div>
        <div class="vote-body">
          <div class="vote-summary">The Appropriation Bill for fiscal year 2023-2024 passed at second reading. The budget included increases to GST from 9% to 15%, increases to the tourism departure tax, and significant capital expenditure commitments. Opposition parties voted against, citing the cost-of-living impact of the GST increase on ordinary households.</div>
          <div class="vote-detail">
            <div class="detail-label">How MPs Voted</div>
            <div class="mp-grid">
              <div class="mp-vote aye"><div class="mp-dot aye"></div><div><div class="mp-name">Sitiveni Rabuka</div><div class="mp-party">PA · PM</div></div></div>
              <div class="mp-vote aye"><div class="mp-dot aye"></div><div><div class="mp-name">Biman Prasad</div><div class="mp-party">NFP · DPM</div></div></div>
              <div class="mp-vote aye"><div class="mp-dot aye"></div><div><div class="mp-name">Manoa Kamikamica</div><div class="mp-party">PA · DPM</div></div></div>
              <div class="mp-vote aye"><div class="mp-dot aye"></div><div><div class="mp-name">Viliame Gavoka</div><div class="mp-party">SODELPA</div></div></div>
              <div class="mp-vote aye"><div class="mp-dot aye"></div><div><div class="mp-name">Lynda Tabuya</div><div class="mp-party">PA</div></div></div>
              <div class="mp-vote no"><div class="mp-dot no"></div><div><div class="mp-name">Inia Seruiratu</div><div class="mp-party">FijiFirst</div></div></div>
              <div class="mp-vote no"><div class="mp-dot no"></div><div><div class="mp-name">Ro Filipe Tuisawau</div><div class="mp-party">FijiFirst</div></div></div>
              <div class="mp-vote no"><div class="mp-dot no"></div><div><div class="mp-name">Premila Kumar</div><div class="mp-party">FijiFirst</div></div></div>
            </div>
            <div class="data-note">⚠ Full division record pending verification from Hansard. Partial data shown. FPR is working to verify complete MP voting records for this division.</div>
            <div class="vote-analysis">
              <div class="vote-analysis-label">FPR Analysis</div>
              The budget passed along coalition lines — People's Alliance, NFP and SODELPA voting together against FijiFirst in opposition. The GST increase from 9% to 15% was the most politically contentious element — a fiscally necessary but politically costly decision that the opposition argued disproportionately burdened lower-income households already struggling with post-COVID cost of living pressures.
            </div>
            <div class="vote-tags">
              <span class="vtag">Budget 2023-24</span><span class="vtag">GST increase</span><span class="vtag">Coalition vote</span><span class="vtag">Cost of living</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- VOTE 2 -->
      <div class="vote-card" data-category="electoral" data-result="passed" data-text="national referendum bill constitutional amendment">
        <div class="vote-header" onclick="toggleVote(this)">
          <span class="vote-date">2025</span>
          <div class="vote-info">
            <div class="vote-title">National Referendum Bill No. 46 — First Reading</div>
            <div class="vote-meta">Electoral · Constitutional</div>
          </div>
          <div class="vote-result">
            <span class="result-badge result-passed">Passed</span>
            <span class="vote-tally">Tally pending verification</span>
          </div>
          <span class="chevron">›</span>
        </div>
        <div class="vote-body">
          <div class="vote-summary">The National Referendum Bill No. 46 of 2025 passed its first reading. The Bill establishes the framework for referenda required to amend the 2013 Constitution. Opposition parties and civil society groups raised concerns about provisions restricting public communication during referendum campaigns.</div>
          <div class="vote-detail">
            <div class="detail-label">How MPs Voted</div>
            <div class="data-note">⚠ Full division record pending verification from Hansard. The FPR is working to extract complete voting records for this bill from parliamentary transcripts.</div>
            <div class="vote-analysis">
              <div class="vote-analysis-label">FPR Analysis</div>
              The National Referendum Bill is among the most significant pieces of legislation in the current parliamentary term — it creates the framework through which Fijians will vote on any constitutional changes the CRC recommends. The bill's communication restrictions raised direct concerns about whether the referendum process it governs will meet the standard of genuine public deliberation a constitutional referendum requires. The FPR's launch article examined these concerns in detail.
            </div>
            <div class="vote-tags">
              <span class="vtag">Referendum Bill</span><span class="vtag">Constitutional reform</span><span class="vtag">Communication restrictions</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- VOTE 3 -->
      <div class="vote-card" data-category="budget" data-result="passed" data-text="2024 budget appropriation supplementary">
        <div class="vote-header" onclick="toggleVote(this)">
          <span class="vote-date">Nov 2024</span>
          <div class="vote-info">
            <div class="vote-title">Appropriation (2024-2025) Bill — Second Reading</div>
            <div class="vote-meta">Budget and finance · Session 2, 2024</div>
          </div>
          <div class="vote-result">
            <span class="result-badge result-passed">Passed</span>
            <span class="vote-tally">Tally pending verification</span>
          </div>
          <span class="chevron">›</span>
        </div>
        <div class="vote-body">
          <div class="vote-summary">The 2024-2025 Appropriation Bill passed. The budget continued fiscal consolidation measures begun in 2023, with the IMF recommending a primary surplus of approximately 2% of GDP by FY2030. Public debt remained elevated at approximately 80% of GDP according to the IMF's June 2025 Article IV consultation.</div>
          <div class="vote-detail">
            <div class="detail-label">How MPs Voted</div>
            <div class="data-note">⚠ Full division record pending verification from Hansard.</div>
            <div class="vote-analysis">
              <div class="vote-analysis-label">FPR Analysis</div>
              The 2024-2025 budget continued the coalition's fiscal consolidation trajectory — necessary given Fiji's elevated debt position but politically challenging given cost-of-living pressures. The FPR's analysis of Fiji's sovereign wealth fund deficit — The Politics of Saving — examines the structural fiscal context in which these budget decisions are made.
            </div>
            <div class="vote-tags">
              <span class="vtag">Budget 2024-25</span><span class="vtag">Fiscal consolidation</span><span class="vtag">IMF</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- VOTE 4 -->
      <div class="vote-card" data-category="governance" data-result="passed" data-text="parliamentary salaries allowances members">
        <div class="vote-header" onclick="toggleVote(this)">
          <span class="vote-date">2024</span>
          <div class="vote-info">
            <div class="vote-title">Parliamentary (Remuneration and Allowances) Amendment</div>
            <div class="vote-meta">Governance · Salaries</div>
          </div>
          <div class="vote-result">
            <span class="result-badge result-passed">Passed</span>
            <span class="vote-tally">Tally pending verification</span>
          </div>
          <span class="chevron">›</span>
        </div>
        <div class="vote-body">
          <div class="vote-summary">Parliament voted to increase the salaries and allowances of members of Parliament — a decision that drew significant public criticism at a time when the government had publicly committed to fiscal restraint and asked ordinary Fijians to absorb the costs of the GST increase. The vote generated public controversy about parliamentary accountability.</div>
          <div class="vote-detail">
            <div class="detail-label">How MPs Voted</div>
            <div class="data-note">⚠ Full division record pending verification from Hansard. This is one of the most important votes to document given its public significance.</div>
            <div class="vote-analysis">
              <div class="vote-analysis-label">FPR Analysis</div>
              The parliamentary salary increase vote is one of the most politically significant of the current term — it directly contradicted the government's public messaging about fiscal discipline and cost-of-living sensitivity. Documenting exactly who voted for the increase, who voted against, and who was absent is a core accountability function of this tracker.
            </div>
            <div class="vote-tags">
              <span class="vtag">Parliamentary salaries</span><span class="vtag">Accountability</span><span class="vtag">Fiscal discipline</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

